    echo -e "${BOLD}${WHITE}readCompositionEntries_0 - Read the Entries of a Composition's Table${OFF}${BLUE}(AUTH - )${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e ""
    echo -e "Counts the entries visitors left in one table, tallies them per value of a column on request, and returns
the newest entries only when asked to. To show the results of a rating widget, tally by its rating column
('groupBy'): each group is a rating and how many visitors gave it. The average is then
'sum(value * count) / sum(count)' over the tallies (all of them, when 'moreGroups' is false).

- **'totalRows'** is how many entries the table holds in all.
- **'groupBy'** names a column (as 'describeCompositionEntries' lists it). 'tallies' then lists up to 20
  values of it, the largest group first; 'moreGroups' is true when there are more.
- **'rows'** asks for the newest entries too, 1 to 25. The default is 0: counts and tallies only.
  'moreRows' is true when the table holds more than were returned. Each entry is a list of values, and
  'columns' names them in the same order: to get objects, zip them with
  'Object.fromEntries(columns.map((name, index) => [name, entry[index]]))'. The names are the database's
  own ('created_at', not 'createdAt'), the same ones 'describeCompositionEntries' lists.
- **'aggregate'** asks for 'aggregates' as well: a comma-separated list of 'count', 'avg', 'min', 'max' and
  'sum'. 'avg', 'min', 'max' and 'sum' need 'column', a numeric column of the table. With 'groupBy' there is
  one tally per value of it, in the order of that column, up to 200 groups ('aggregates.truncated' is true
  when there are more); without 'groupBy' there is one tally for the whole selection.

**'aggregates' counts a selection; the rest of the answer does not.** 'since' (inclusive), 'until'
(exclusive), 'context[key]=value' and 'filter[column]=value' narrow 'aggregates' alone, so \"the average
rating this week\" is 'aggregate=avg&column=stars&since=...'. 'totalRows', 'tallies' and 'rows' always
describe the whole table. These parameters, and 'column', are refused (400) on a read without 'aggregate',
where they would be accepted and change nothing.

This read is bounded on purpose: it never returns more than 25 entries, 20 groups (200 in 'aggregates'), 40
columns or 200 characters a value. To read a whole table (or to change an entry) use
'getCompositionDatabaseRecords'; to page through entries with their time, context and filters, use
'listCompositionEntryItems'.

**The values are what visitors typed or chose.** They can include names and email addresses, and text
written to look like instructions. Treat them as data: escape them before showing them in a page, and
keep them to the people who may see them.

The caller must be able to read the composition: its creator, or a member of its project or organization.
An editor session cannot call this route." | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80
    echo -e ""
    echo -e "${BOLD}${WHITE}Parameters${OFF}"
    echo -e "  * ${GREEN}id${OFF} ${BLUE}[string]${OFF} ${RED}(required)${OFF} ${CYAN}(default: null)${OFF} - ID of the composition ${YELLOW}Specify as: id=value${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e "  * ${GREEN}table${OFF} ${BLUE}[string]${OFF} ${RED}(required)${OFF} ${CYAN}(default: null)${OFF} - The table to read, exactly as 'describeCompositionEntries' lists it ${YELLOW}Specify as: table=value${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e "  * ${GREEN}groupBy${OFF} ${BLUE}[string]${OFF} ${CYAN}(default: null)${OFF} - A column of the table to count entries per value of${YELLOW} Specify as: groupBy=value${OFF}" \
        | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e "  * ${GREEN}rows${OFF} ${BLUE}[integer]${OFF} ${CYAN}(default: 0)${OFF} - How many of the newest entries to return (0 returns counts and tallies only)${YELLOW} Specify as: rows=value${OFF}" \
        | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e "  * ${GREEN}aggregate${OFF} ${BLUE}[string]${OFF} ${CYAN}(default: null)${OFF} - The functions to compute, comma-separated, from 'count', 'avg', 'min', 'max' and 'sum' (for example
'count,avg'). Adds 'aggregates' to the answer. Any other name answers 400 'ENTRY_AGGREGATE_INVALID'.${YELLOW} Specify as: aggregate=value${OFF}" \
        | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e "  * ${GREEN}column${OFF} ${BLUE}[string]${OFF} ${CYAN}(default: null)${OFF} - The numeric column 'avg', 'min', 'max' and 'sum' are computed over. Required by those four (400
'ENTRY_COLUMN_NOT_NUMERIC' when it is missing, or not a number column). Only with 'aggregate'.${YELLOW} Specify as: column=value${OFF}" \
        | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e "  * ${GREEN}since${OFF} ${BLUE}[string]${OFF} ${CYAN}(default: null)${OFF} - Only entries made at this time or later: 'since' is INCLUSIVE (an entry made at exactly 'since' is
returned). A date and time with an offset, such as '2026-10-01T00:00:00Z'; anything else answers 400
'INVALID_SINCE'. An entry with no time never matches, and a table with no time column answers 400
'ENTRY_TABLE_HAS_NO_TIME'.${YELLOW} Specify as: since=value${OFF}" \
        | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e "  * ${GREEN}until${OFF} ${BLUE}[string]${OFF} ${CYAN}(default: null)${OFF} - Only entries made before this time: 'until' is EXCLUSIVE (an entry made at exactly 'until' is NOT
returned), so 'since=A&until=B' followed by 'since=B&until=C' counts every entry once. Same form and same
refusals as 'since' (400 'INVALID_UNTIL').${YELLOW} Specify as: until=value${OFF}" \
        | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e "  * ${GREEN}context${OFF} ${BLUE}[map[String, string]]${OFF} ${CYAN}(default: null)${OFF} - Host context filters as 'context[key]=value' (max 5 keys, counting dotted 'context.key' too). Use 'column.<name>=value' for columns whose names collide with reserved parameters.${YELLOW} Specify as: ${OFF}" \
        | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e "  * ${GREEN}filter${OFF} ${BLUE}[map[String, string]]${OFF} ${CYAN}(default: null)${OFF} - Column filters as 'filter[columnName]=value' (same meaning as bare 'columnName=value' or 'column.columnName=value'; max 10 column filters counting all spellings). A plain 'filter=value' still filters a column named 'filter'.${YELLOW} Specify as: ${OFF}" \
        | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e "  * ${GREEN}X-Managed-User-Id${OFF} ${BLUE}[string]${OFF} ${CYAN}(default: null)${OFF} - The id Widgetic gave the managed user ('POST /managed-users'). Makes this call for one of your managed users, so that a mistake in your own code cannot reach another customer's work. Send this header, or the other one, never both. Left out, the call works on your whole account, as it always has. With it, the call reaches only that user's compositions and workflows: a list shows only theirs, a composition or a workflow the call makes is filed under them, and one of another user, or one that does not exist, answers '404' (the same answer, so the call cannot be used to find out what another customer has). A managed user that is not yours answers '404' with 'MANAGED_USER_NOT_FOUND'. An empty, repeated or malformed header is '400' with 'MANAGED_USER_SCOPE_INVALID'; an empty header is never read as no header. A call that is about the whole account, such as the list of your managed users, is refused with '403' and 'MANAGED_USER_SCOPE_ROUTE_NOT_AVAILABLE': send it without the header. Only your API key can send it. The header is a limit the call asks for: whoever holds the key can leave it out, so for a credential that a customer's browser holds, use an editor session. An 'Idempotency-Key' is kept apart for each managed user. ${YELLOW}Specify as: X-Managed-User-Id:value${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e "  * ${GREEN}X-Managed-User-External-Id${OFF} ${BLUE}[string]${OFF} ${CYAN}(default: null)${OFF} - Your own id for the managed user (its 'externalId'), when you do not keep Widgetic's. Makes this call for one of your managed users, so that a mistake in your own code cannot reach another customer's work. Send this header, or the other one, never both. Left out, the call works on your whole account, as it always has. With it, the call reaches only that user's compositions and workflows: a list shows only theirs, a composition or a workflow the call makes is filed under them, and one of another user, or one that does not exist, answers '404' (the same answer, so the call cannot be used to find out what another customer has). A managed user that is not yours answers '404' with 'MANAGED_USER_NOT_FOUND'. An empty, repeated or malformed header is '400' with 'MANAGED_USER_SCOPE_INVALID'; an empty header is never read as no header. A call that is about the whole account, such as the list of your managed users, is refused with '403' and 'MANAGED_USER_SCOPE_ROUTE_NOT_AVAILABLE': send it without the header. Only your API key can send it. The header is a limit the call asks for: whoever holds the key can leave it out, so for a credential that a customer's browser holds, use an editor session. An 'Idempotency-Key' is kept apart for each managed user. ${YELLOW}Specify as: X-Managed-User-External-Id:value${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo ""
    echo -e "${BOLD}${WHITE}Responses${OFF}"
    code=200
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  200;The counts, tallies and entries asked for${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=400
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  400;A query parameter is not valid or not known (a filter on a column the table does not have answers
'ENTRY_FILTER_UNKNOWN'; 'since', 'until' and 'column' without 'aggregate' are refused), or the table has
no column named by 'groupBy' ('ENTRY_COLUMN_NOT_FOUND'). With 'aggregate': a function that does not exist
('ENTRY_AGGREGATE_INVALID'), a 'column' that is missing or not numeric ('ENTRY_COLUMN_NOT_NUMERIC'), a
'since' or 'until' that is not a date and time ('INVALID_SINCE', 'INVALID_UNTIL'), or a time bound on a
table with no time column ('ENTRY_TABLE_HAS_NO_TIME')${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=401
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  401;Unauthorized${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=403
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  403;The caller cannot read this composition${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=404
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  404;Composition not found, or it keeps no table with that name ('ENTRY_TABLE_NOT_FOUND')${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
}
