    code=400
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  400;Invalid input${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=401
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  401;Unauthorized${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=403
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  403;Forbidden - the caller is not a partner, or 'managerId' names another manager (a partner can create managed users only for themselves)${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=409
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  409;A managed user with this 'externalId' already exists for this manager. External ids are unique per manager, so this never refers to another partner's record.${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
}
##############################################################################
#
# Print help for createManagedUserEditorSession operation
#
##############################################################################
print_createManagedUserEditorSession_help() {
    echo ""
    echo -e "${BOLD}${WHITE}createManagedUserEditorSession - Create an editor session for a managed user${OFF}${BLUE}(AUTH - )${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e ""
    echo -e "Makes a short-lived credential that lets the browser of ONE of your managed users use Widgetic's editor
pieces, such as the File Browser and the composition editor, without your API key ever reaching that
browser. Call this from your server when the page that hosts the editor opens, and hand the 'token' in
the answer to that page.

The token is shown once. It starts with 'wgt_ses_' and the browser sends it as
'Authorization: Bearer <token>'. It can do only what the 'surfaces' you name allow, and only for this
managed user:

- 'files': upload a file ('uploadsPost') and list the files uploaded for this user ('uploadsGet'). Every
  file is filed for this user and stored in your own storage destination, never in Widgetic's: a file a
  customer uploads is yours to keep, and takes none of your storage allowance. Partner storage is not
  optional, so no session, whatever its surfaces, can be made until you have set a destination
  ('setPartnerStorageDestination'); until then it is refused with 409 and 'PARTNER_STORAGE_REQUIRED', and
  when the destination cannot be used with 503 and 'STORAGE_DESTINATION_UNAVAILABLE'. A destination you
  remove after the session was made stops its uploads too (the same 409; the browser is only told that
  the feature is not available right now). To keep a customer from uploading, leave 'files' out of the
  session and hand the editors your own media library instead ('mediaLibrary').
- 'editor': edit one of this user's compositions: read it ('getCompositionById', its content, design,
  embed settings and schemas), check a content change ('validateCompositionContent'), and change its
  name, content, design and embed settings ('updateComposition', 'setDynamicContent'). For a widget that
  answers visitors' questions from documents (the 'ai-answers' adapter), it also lists those documents,
  adds one as text or as a file (a text file or a picture; a PDF once PDFs are read), and removes one
  ('getAiAnswersKnowledge', 'addAiAnswersKnowledgeDocument', 'addAiAnswersKnowledgeFile',
  'removeAiAnswersKnowledgeDocument'); adding costs no credits, and is limited for each of your users
  separately. It can reach
  only compositions you created for this managed user (tag them with 'managedUserId' when you create
  them); any other composition, including another of your users', answers 404.
- 'creator': use Widgetic's widget creator for this user, including its AI. Draw on canvases and save
  them ('getAllCanvases', 'getCanvas', 'createCanvas', 'updateCanvas', 'previewDeleteCanvas',
  'deleteCanvas'); make, change, copy and delete the widgets on them ('createWidget', 'getWidgets',
  'getWidgetsBatch', 'updateWidget', 'uploadWidgetThumbnail', 'duplicateWidget', 'deleteWidget');
  list and make the compositions of a widget it built ('getAllCompositions', 'createComposition'), which
  is how it shows the widget with sample values; keep the
  conversation of each widget ('getConversationsByWidgetId', 'createConversationForWidget',
  'updateConversation', 'getMessages', 'createMessage', 'updateMessage', 'restoreCheckpoint'); and read a
  widget's schemas and give it its repository ('getWidgetContentSchema', 'getWidgetDesignSchema',
  'updateWidgetRepository'). The AI that builds a widget is part of it: list the models
  ('agentModelsGet'), open the widget's repository ('agentRepositoriesPost',
  'agentRepositoriesRepoIdGet'), start a generation and follow or cancel it ('agentCodeGeneratePost',
  'operationsStreamGet', 'operationsIdGet', 'operationsIdCancelPost'), build and preview the result
  ('agentWidgetBuilderRepoHeadWidgetIdGet', 'buildWidgetFromRepo', 'previewWidgetVersion'), publish a
  version of the widget and move between its versions ('agentWidgetBuilderPublishWidgetIdPost',
  'getWidgetPublishHistory', 'setWidgetPublishHistoryLive', 'renameWidgetPublishHistoryTitle'), and
  turn a stroke or a sentence into a decision ('agentShapeRecognizePost', 'agentDesignResolvePost'). It can
  also offer the customer your presets as starting points: read them and ask for a copy for this customer
  ('listMyPresets', 'copyMyPreset'; you choose the presets with 'setPartnerPreset').
  What the session makes is filed for this managed user, and the lists it reads hold only this user's
  canvases, widgets and compositions. It can reach only canvases, widgets, compositions, repositories,
  uploaded files and operations made for this managed user (tag the canvases and widgets you create
  with 'managedUserId'); any other canvas, widget, composition, conversation, message, repository, file
  or operation, including another of your users', answers 404. The creator also saves the composition
  it is editing ('updateComposition', from the 'editor' surface) and attaches pictures to its chat
  ('uploadsPost', from the 'files' surface), and the surfaces do not imply one another: to open the
  whole creator for a user, ask for 'creator', 'editor' and 'files' together. A generation or a build
  one user starts can be followed and cancelled by that user and by you, never by another of your
  users. The AI is paid for by your account, as your own calls are: its credits and allowances are
  yours. A session cannot make a widget public (publishing a version does not), file one under a
  project or an organization, or set anything the creator does not set: a body with another field is
  refused with 403 and 'EDITOR_SESSION_FIELD_NOT_ALLOWED'.
- 'workflows': use Widgetic's Workflows editor for this user. List their workflows and the compositions
  a workflow of theirs can chain ('listWorkspaceWorkflows', 'listWorkspaceWorkflowCompositionOptions');
  list the starting points you offer them and make a workflow from one, which gives the user their own copy
  of every widget it chains, a composition of their own on each copy, and a draft
  ('listWorkspaceWorkflowPresets', 'createWorkspaceWorkflowFromPreset'; you offer them with
  'setPartnerWorkflowPreset');
  make, open, change and delete one ('createWorkspaceWorkflow', 'getWorkspaceWorkflow',
  'saveWorkspaceWorkflow', 'deleteWorkspaceWorkflow') and copy it ('duplicateWorkspaceWorkflow'); publish
  it or discard the changes of its draft ('publishWorkspaceWorkflow',
  'discardWorkspaceWorkflowChanges'); read and restore its versions ('listWorkspaceWorkflowVersions',
  'getWorkspaceWorkflowVersion', 'restoreWorkspaceWorkflowVersion'); pause, resume, archive and unarchive it
  ('pauseWorkspaceWorkflow', 'resumeWorkspaceWorkflow', 'archiveWorkspaceWorkflow',
  'unarchiveWorkspaceWorkflow'); and read its counts ('getWorkspaceWorkflowStats'). The workspace in each
  path is 'personal': a session has no other, and a path that names an organization is refused. What the
  session makes is filed for this managed user ('managedUserId'), the lists hold only this user's workflows,
  and it can reach only workflows made for this managed user; any other workflow, including one of yours
  or of another of your users, answers 404. A workflow can chain only the compositions you made for this
  managed user (tag them with 'managedUserId'): one that belongs to anybody else is not available, and
  publishing a workflow that uses it is refused. A customer can have at most 50 workflows, and what a
  customer's session reads never says who published a version. A session cannot set who a workflow belongs
  to or which workspace it is in: a body with another field is refused with 403 and
  'EDITOR_SESSION_FIELD_NOT_ALLOWED'.

Everything else is refused with 403 and 'EDITOR_SESSION_ROUTE_NOT_ALLOWED': a session cannot read your
account, make more sessions, change your presets or delete a composition, and a session without the 'creator' surface cannot
create or list compositions. Create the composition yourself with your API key, then open the editor on it.

A session ends at 'expiresAt' (at most four hours), when you end it ('revokeManagedUserEditorSession'),
or when the managed user is switched off or deleted. A managed user can have at most 100 live sessions at
once ('429 EDITOR_SESSION_LIMIT_REACHED'). A session that is bound to a web page ('allowedOrigin') is
refused from any other origin.

The AI the session runs is paid for with your credits. Set 'maxCredits' to hold the session to a number
of them: once its generations have taken that many (a generation that fails is refunded and does not
count), the next one is refused with 402 and 'EDITOR_SESSION_CREDIT_LIMIT_REACHED', and the browser is told
only that the feature is not available right now. Without it, the limit Widgetic has set for your account
applies when it has set one (the same limit for every session you make, and 'maxCredits: null' asks for
none), and otherwise the credits of your account are the only ceiling. What each of your users' sessions
has spent is in 'getManagedUserUsage'.

Each call makes a new session. It does not take an 'Idempotency-Key': the answer holds the token, and
the token is never stored where a retry could read it back. The answer is sent with
'Cache-Control: no-store'." | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80
    echo -e ""
    echo -e "${BOLD}${WHITE}Parameters${OFF}"
    echo -e "  * ${GREEN}id${OFF} ${BLUE}[string]${OFF} ${RED}(required)${OFF} ${CYAN}(default: null)${OFF} - The managed user the session is for (Widgetic's id for the user) ${YELLOW}Specify as: id=value${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e "  * ${GREEN}body${OFF} ${BLUE}[application/json]${OFF} ${RED}(required)${OFF}${OFF} - " | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e ""
    echo ""
    echo -e "${BOLD}${WHITE}Responses${OFF}"
    code=201
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  201;The session, with its token (shown once)${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=400
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  400;A surface is not one that exists, 'expiresInSeconds' or 'maxCredits' is out of range, or 'allowedOrigin' is not an origin${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=401
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  401;Unauthorized${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=403
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  403;Forbidden - the caller is not a partner, or Widgetic has switched editor sessions off for your account ('EDITOR_SESSIONS_DISABLED_FOR_PARTNER')${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=404
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  404;No managed user with this id on your account ('MANAGED_USER_NOT_FOUND'). Another partner's managed user answers 404 as well.${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=409
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  409;The managed user is switched off, so no session can be made for it ('MANAGED_USER_INACTIVE'); or you have not set a storage destination ('PARTNER_STORAGE_REQUIRED')${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=429
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  429;The managed user already has the most live sessions allowed ('EDITOR_SESSION_LIMIT_REACHED')${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=503
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  503;Editor sessions are switched off for the moment ('EDITOR_SESSIONS_DISABLED'), or your storage destination cannot be used ('STORAGE_DESTINATION_UNAVAILABLE'). Try again later.${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
}
##############################################################################
#
# Print help for createPartnerExtraCreditsInvoice operation
#
##############################################################################
print_createPartnerExtraCreditsInvoice_help() {
    echo ""
    echo -e "${BOLD}${WHITE}createPartnerExtraCreditsInvoice - Buy extra credits for a partner${OFF}${BLUE}(AUTH - )${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e ""
    echo -e "Asks Widgetic for an invoice for extra credits, on top of the credits of the contract. Name the dollars; the
invoice is for the most whole credits they buy at the **list price** of a credit (the price a contract may
lower belongs to the contract), so it is never for more than you asked: 12.34 buys 123 credits and the invoice
says 12.30. The smallest purchase is 10 dollars and one request buys at most 100000 (ask Widgetic for an
invoice for more).

Pay the invoice with the link in the answer. When it is paid the credits are added **once, for good**, to the
account of the person who administers the partner, which is the account everything the partner builds is
charged to ('getPartnerCreditBalance' shows it). Extra credits **do not expire**, unlike the credits of a
contract period, which end with it. Nothing is added before the invoice is paid, and an unpaid invoice for
extra credits never stops the partner: only an unpaid invoice of the contract does ('payment_arrears').

Available only to partners that have an active paid contract in force with Widgetic ('NO_PAID_CONTRACT' when
none is in force) and no overdue contract invoice ('CONTRACT_INVOICE_OVERDUE' while a contract invoice is past
its due day). A partner that has run out of credits during its period can buy more at the list price.

An 'Idempotency-Key' is required, and it is what makes a retry safe: the same key with the same body returns
the invoice already issued, the same key with a different body is refused with 422, and a duplicate that
arrives while the first is still running is refused with 409. Use one key per purchase you mean to make, and
a new key for the next one. At most 10 requests an hour.

Who may ask: the person who administers the partner, or a Widgetic administrator. A key limited to scopes
needs 'billing:write'." | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80
    echo -e ""
    echo -e "${BOLD}${WHITE}Parameters${OFF}"
    echo -e "  * ${GREEN}partnerId${OFF} ${BLUE}[string]${OFF} ${RED}(required)${OFF} ${CYAN}(default: null)${OFF} - Partner ID ${YELLOW}Specify as: partnerId=value${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e "  * ${GREEN}Idempotency-Key${OFF} ${BLUE}[string]${OFF} ${RED}(required)${OFF} ${CYAN}(default: null)${OFF} - A key of your own for this purchase, so that a retry cannot make a second invoice ${YELLOW}Specify as: Idempotency-Key:value${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e "  * ${GREEN}body${OFF} ${BLUE}[application/json]${OFF} ${RED}(required)${OFF}${OFF} - " | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e ""
    echo ""
    echo -e "${BOLD}${WHITE}Responses${OFF}"
    code=200
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  200;The invoice was issued${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=400
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  400;The amount is not a number of dollars and cents, is under 10 or over 100000, or the Idempotency-Key header is missing or malformed${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=401
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  401;Not authenticated${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=403
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  403;The caller does not administer this partner${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=404
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  404;There is no such partner (a Widgetic administrator asked for an id that does not exist)${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=409
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  409;Another request with this Idempotency-Key is still running${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=422
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  422;This Idempotency-Key was already used with a different body, the partner has no active paid contract ('NO_PAID_CONTRACT'), the partner owes an overdue contract invoice ('CONTRACT_INVOICE_OVERDUE'), the partner has no administrator account to add the credits to ('NO_PARTNER_ADMINISTRATOR'), there is no billing email and no contact email to send the invoice to ('NO_BILLING_EMAIL'), or Stripe did not accept the tax ID on the billing profile ('TAX_ID_INVALID')${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=429
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  429;Too many requests; at most 10 an hour${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=503
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  503;Stripe could not issue the invoice. Nothing was sent; retry with the same Idempotency-Key.${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
}
##############################################################################
#
# Print help for createPublicCompositionEntry operation
#
##############################################################################
print_createPublicCompositionEntry_help() {
    echo ""
    echo -e "${BOLD}${WHITE}createPublicCompositionEntry - Append a visitor entry through the gateway${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e ""
    echo -e "Public append-only write into a published composition database. No API key. The browser must send a permitted 'Origin' header: the artifact iframe origin, or any website when the owner has not restricted the allowed websites (when the owner has, one of the websites the owner listed, Widgetic's own sites, the visitor's own machine or the owner's own platform). When the request comes from the shared artifact origin, it must also carry the per-composition write token ('X-Widgetic-Write-Token' header or 'writeToken' body field, handed to the widget in 'widgetic:host' as 'entries.writeToken' and returned as 'entryWriteToken' on 'getPublicCompositionEmbed'). Host 'context' is stored for partner attribution; it is not authenticated unless the partner signs it (see **Signed context**). Request bodies are limited to 16 KB before parsing.
**Address.** 'https://api.widgetic.com/embed/compositions/{compositionId}/entries/{table}': the root of the API host, NOT under '/v1'. A client generated from this description for 'https://api.widgetic.com/v1' must be given the base address 'https://api.widgetic.com' for the calls of the 'Public Embed' tag.
**Signed context.** A partner that wants to trust 'context' (to bill a customer by it, say) makes a signing secret ('rotatePartnerEntryContextSecret'), and its server signs the context it hands to the embed. The signature travels inside 'context' as two reserved keys, 'widgetic_exp' (UTC seconds, at most seven days ahead) and 'widgetic_sig'. The gateway checks them after the 'Origin' and before anything else is judged, stored or announced, and keeps and announces the context WITHOUT them. A context that is not signed as the partner requires is refused with 403 'CONTEXT_SIGNATURE_REQUIRED', 'CONTEXT_SIGNATURE_INVALID' or 'CONTEXT_SIGNATURE_EXPIRED'; when the check cannot be made just now the answer is a retryable 503 'CONTEXT_SIGNATURE_UNAVAILABLE', never an unchecked entry. Until a partner makes a secret nothing changes: the two keys are dropped and the rest is taken as it came. A signature is good until its 'widgetic_exp' and may be used again until then, so a partner that must count each submission once keeps a unique value of its own (a 'submissionId', say) in the context. The recipe and a test vector are in the description of 'rotatePartnerEntryContextSecret'." | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80
    echo -e ""
    echo -e "${BOLD}${WHITE}Parameters${OFF}"
    echo -e "  * ${GREEN}compositionId${OFF} ${BLUE}[string]${OFF} ${RED}(required)${OFF} ${CYAN}(default: null)${OFF} -  ${YELLOW}Specify as: compositionId=value${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e "  * ${GREEN}table${OFF} ${BLUE}[string]${OFF} ${RED}(required)${OFF} ${CYAN}(default: null)${OFF} -  ${YELLOW}Specify as: table=value${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e "  * ${GREEN}X-Widgetic-Write-Token${OFF} ${BLUE}[string]${OFF} ${CYAN}(default: null)${OFF} - Signed per-composition write token handed to the widget in 'widgetic:host' as 'entries.writeToken' (and returned by 'GET /embed/compositions/{compositionId}' as 'entryWriteToken'). Required when the request comes from the shared Widgetic artifact origin; verified whenever present. ${YELLOW}Specify as: X-Widgetic-Write-Token:value${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e "  * ${GREEN}X-Widgetic-Visitor-Id${OFF} ${BLUE}[string]${OFF} ${CYAN}(default: null)${OFF} - A random id the widget's browser makes once and keeps (16 to 64 characters of 'A-Za-z0-9_-'), sent so a table's per-visitor 'limit' (declared in the widget database file) can count this browser. Not an identity and not a secret. Without it, or with a malformed value, the limit counts only by network address. ${YELLOW}Specify as: X-Widgetic-Visitor-Id:value${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e "  * ${GREEN}body${OFF} ${BLUE}[application/json]${OFF} ${RED}(required)${OFF}${OFF} - " | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e ""
    echo ""
    echo -e "${BOLD}${WHITE}Responses${OFF}"
    code=201
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  201;Entry stored${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=400
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  400;Invalid body or values ('ENTRY_BODY_INVALID', 'ENTRY_VALUE_INVALID', 'ENTRY_CONTEXT_INVALID')${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=403
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  403;Origin not allowed ('ORIGIN_NOT_ALLOWED'), per-composition write token missing, invalid or expired ('WRITE_TOKEN_REQUIRED', 'WRITE_TOKEN_INVALID', 'WRITE_TOKEN_EXPIRED'), or the context is not signed as the partner requires ('CONTEXT_SIGNATURE_REQUIRED', 'CONTEXT_SIGNATURE_INVALID', 'CONTEXT_SIGNATURE_EXPIRED')${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=404
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  404;Composition unavailable or table not found${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=413
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  413;Body too large ('PAYLOAD_TOO_LARGE')${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=415
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  415;Not JSON ('UNSUPPORTED_MEDIA_TYPE')${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=422
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  422;Row rejected ('ENTRY_ROW_REJECTED')${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=429
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  429;Rate limited ('RATE_LIMITED'), always with 'Retry-After'. Three limits answer this way: 20 entries a minute per visitor address and composition, 300 a minute per composition, and a day's allowance per composition (default 50,000 stored entries in 24 hours; 'details.scope' is 'composition_daily' for that one). Only an entry that was stored counts against the day's allowance. A fourth answers a table that declares a per-visitor 'limit': 'error.code' is 'ENTRY_LIMIT_REACHED', 'details.scope' is 'visitor_limit' (this browser) or 'address_limit' (this network address), and 'details.perVisitor' and 'details.per' repeat what the table declares.${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=503
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  503;Database unavailable or statement timeout, or the gateway could not tell just now whether the context must be signed ('CONTEXT_SIGNATURE_UNAVAILABLE'). Try again.${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
}
##############################################################################
#
# Print help for createUserApiKey operation
#
##############################################################################
print_createUserApiKey_help() {
    echo ""
    echo -e "${BOLD}${WHITE}createUserApiKey - Create an API key${OFF}${BLUE}(AUTH - )${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e ""
    echo -e "Makes a new API key for an account and returns its secret in 'key'. That is the only time the secret is shown: Widgetic keeps a hash, so a key that was not stored cannot be recovered, only replaced. To rotate a key, make the new one, switch the integration over to it, then delete the old one.
Only a person signed in on widgetic.com can make a key: a request made with an API key, or with an SDK token, is refused with 403. That way a leaked key cannot be used to make a second one that survives its revocation. Make keys from the dashboard; a key can still list, rename, switch off and delete keys.
An 'Idempotency-Key' header is required (8 to 50 characters: letters, digits, '-' and '_'). A retry with the same header and the same body returns the same answer instead of making a second key, and the same header with a different body is refused with 422. Make keys one at a time: two requests for the same account that run at the same moment can overwrite each other.
A key can be limited to what it needs. Send a 'preset' ('read_only', 'content' or 'full_access') or a list of 'scopes', never both. Send neither for a key that can do everything its owner can, as every key made before scopes existed. A limited key is refused with 403 and the code 'API_KEY_SCOPE_MISSING' on anything outside its scopes, so a key held by a build server or by a partner's backend can be given only the part of the API it uses. The scopes of a key are fixed when it is made: to widen one, make a new key and delete the old one. A limited key cannot make, change or delete keys, exchange tokens or reach the administration routes. The list of scopes is in the 'ApiKeyScope' schema.
Accounts with API access (Solo, Teams and partner accounts) have no limit on how many keys they hold. An account on a plan without API access cannot make one (a partner account is not asked about a plan)." | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80
    echo -e ""
    echo -e "${BOLD}${WHITE}Parameters${OFF}"
    echo -e "  * ${GREEN}id${OFF} ${BLUE}[string]${OFF} ${RED}(required)${OFF} ${CYAN}(default: null)${OFF} - The account the key is for. For your own, your own user id ${YELLOW}Specify as: id=value${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e "  * ${GREEN}Idempotency-Key${OFF} ${BLUE}[string]${OFF} ${RED}(required)${OFF} ${CYAN}(default: null)${OFF} - Required: a call without it is refused with '400'. A key of your own that names this one request; a UUID is ideal. It is 8 to 50 characters of letters, digits, '-' and '_'. Send the same key again when you retry (after a timeout, a dropped connection or a '5xx') and the call is carried out once: the retry gets the first answer back, marked 'X-Idempotency-Cached: true'. The same key with a different body is refused with '422', and a retry that arrives while the first call is still running with '409' (see 'Retry-After'). ${YELLOW}Specify as: Idempotency-Key:value${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e "  * ${GREEN}body${OFF} ${BLUE}[application/json]${OFF} ${RED}(required)${OFF}${OFF} - " | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e ""
    echo ""
    echo -e "${BOLD}${WHITE}Responses${OFF}"
    code=200
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  200;The key was made. The secret is in 'key', and is not shown again${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=400
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  400;The name, the expiry or the scopes are not valid (an unknown scope, an empty list, or both a preset and scopes), or the Idempotency-Key header is missing or malformed${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=401
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  401;Not authenticated${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=403
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  403;The request was made with an API key or an SDK token (only a person signed in on widgetic.com can make a key), the account belongs to someone else, or its plan does not include API keys${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=409
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  409;Another request with this Idempotency-Key is still running${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=422
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  422;This Idempotency-Key was already used with a different body${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
}
##############################################################################
#
# Print help for createWidget operation
#
##############################################################################
print_createWidget_help() {
    echo ""
    echo -e "${BOLD}${WHITE}createWidget - Create Widget${OFF}${BLUE}(AUTH - )${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e ""
    echo -e "Creates a widget for your account: a named record with a type and some starting content, on a canvas of
its own (or one of yours that you name). It costs no credits and has no code yet; the code is generated for
it afterwards. The new widget is yours, and you can list it with 'getWidgets'. A widget is a draft until
you say otherwise ('isDraft: false').

If a step after the widget was saved does not go through, the widget is still created, and
'data.warnings' says what did not. Read it before relying on the widget.

A widget can be placed on one of your canvases ('canvasId'), in a project you can edit ('projectId') or in an
organization where you may create widgets ('organizationId'). Naming anything you cannot use is refused
with 403, and the answer is the same whether it exists or not.

To make the widget for one of your managed users, send 'managedUserId' or 'managedUserExternalId'. The widget
stays in your account and is yours to edit; the tag lets you list one user's widgets with 'getWidgets'. The
managed user must be yours and active: one that is not yours, or does not exist, is answered with 404 and
'MANAGED_USER_NOT_FOUND', and one that is switched off with 409 and 'MANAGED_USER_INACTIVE'. The tag is set
here and does not change afterwards.

This call has a limit of its own: 120 per minute for each account (ask Widgetic if you need more). Past
that the call is answered with 429 and a 'Retry-After'. A widget has no database of its own: what the
visitors of a composition leave is kept in the tables of that composition, made when the composition is.
The 'Idempotency-Key' header is required; send the same key when you retry, so one widget is created, not
two." | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80
    echo -e ""
    echo -e "${BOLD}${WHITE}Parameters${OFF}"
    echo -e "  * ${GREEN}Idempotency-Key${OFF} ${BLUE}[string]${OFF} ${RED}(required)${OFF} ${CYAN}(default: null)${OFF} - A unique value (a UUID is fine) that makes a retry of this request safe. ${YELLOW}Specify as: Idempotency-Key:value${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e "  * ${GREEN}body${OFF} ${BLUE}[application/json]${OFF} ${RED}(required)${OFF}${OFF} - " | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e ""
    echo ""
    echo -e "${BOLD}${WHITE}Responses${OFF}"
    code=201
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  201;Widget created successfully${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=400
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  400;Invalid request, or the 'Idempotency-Key' header is missing.${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=401
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  401;Unauthorized${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=403
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  403;The key's role may not use this endpoint, or 'canvasId', 'projectId' or 'organizationId' names
something you may not use.${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=404
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  404;The managed user named by 'managedUserId' or 'managedUserExternalId' is not one of yours ('MANAGED_USER_NOT_FOUND').${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=409
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  409;The managed user is switched off, so nothing new can be made for it ('MANAGED_USER_INACTIVE').${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=429
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  429;Too many widgets created in a minute. See the Retry-After header.${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
}
##############################################################################
#
# Print help for createWorkspaceWorkflow operation
#
##############################################################################
print_createWorkspaceWorkflow_help() {
    echo ""
    echo -e "${BOLD}${WHITE}createWorkspaceWorkflow - Create a Workflow${OFF}${BLUE}(AUTH - )${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e ""
    echo -e "Makes a draft workflow. Give it a composition and the workflow is born with one block, which starts it; without
one it starts empty. A workspace holds up to 500 workflows.
For personal workspace, use 'personal' as workspaceId.
For organization workspace, use the organization UUID as workspaceId. Any active member can create one." | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80
    echo -e ""
    echo -e "${BOLD}${WHITE}Parameters${OFF}"
    echo -e "  * ${GREEN}workspaceId${OFF} ${BLUE}[string]${OFF} ${RED}(required)${OFF} ${CYAN}(default: null)${OFF} - The workspace: 'personal' for your own workspace, or the UUID of an organization. A call made for one of your
managed users ('X-Managed-User-Id') always uses 'personal': a managed user has no other workspace, and a call
that names an organization is refused with 403. ${YELLOW}Specify as: workspaceId=value${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e "  * ${GREEN}Idempotency-Key${OFF} ${BLUE}[string]${OFF} ${RED}(required)${OFF} ${CYAN}(default: null)${OFF} - Required: a call without it is refused with '400'. A key of your own that names this one request; a UUID is ideal. It is 8 to 50 characters of letters, digits, '-' and '_'. Send the same key again when you retry (after a timeout, a dropped connection or a '5xx') and the call is carried out once: the retry gets the first answer back, marked 'X-Idempotency-Cached: true'. The same key with a different body is refused with '422', and a retry that arrives while the first call is still running with '409' (see 'Retry-After'). ${YELLOW}Specify as: Idempotency-Key:value${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e "  * ${GREEN}X-Managed-User-Id${OFF} ${BLUE}[string]${OFF} ${CYAN}(default: null)${OFF} - The id Widgetic gave the managed user ('POST /managed-users'). Makes this call for one of your managed users, so that a mistake in your own code cannot reach another customer's work. Send this header, or the other one, never both. Left out, the call works on your whole account, as it always has. With it, the call reaches only that user's compositions and workflows: a list shows only theirs, a composition or a workflow the call makes is filed under them, and one of another user, or one that does not exist, answers '404' (the same answer, so the call cannot be used to find out what another customer has). A managed user that is not yours answers '404' with 'MANAGED_USER_NOT_FOUND'. An empty, repeated or malformed header is '400' with 'MANAGED_USER_SCOPE_INVALID'; an empty header is never read as no header. A call that is about the whole account, such as the list of your managed users, is refused with '403' and 'MANAGED_USER_SCOPE_ROUTE_NOT_AVAILABLE': send it without the header. Only your API key can send it. The header is a limit the call asks for: whoever holds the key can leave it out, so for a credential that a customer's browser holds, use an editor session. An 'Idempotency-Key' is kept apart for each managed user. ${YELLOW}Specify as: X-Managed-User-Id:value${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e "  * ${GREEN}X-Managed-User-External-Id${OFF} ${BLUE}[string]${OFF} ${CYAN}(default: null)${OFF} - Your own id for the managed user (its 'externalId'), when you do not keep Widgetic's. Makes this call for one of your managed users, so that a mistake in your own code cannot reach another customer's work. Send this header, or the other one, never both. Left out, the call works on your whole account, as it always has. With it, the call reaches only that user's compositions and workflows: a list shows only theirs, a composition or a workflow the call makes is filed under them, and one of another user, or one that does not exist, answers '404' (the same answer, so the call cannot be used to find out what another customer has). A managed user that is not yours answers '404' with 'MANAGED_USER_NOT_FOUND'. An empty, repeated or malformed header is '400' with 'MANAGED_USER_SCOPE_INVALID'; an empty header is never read as no header. A call that is about the whole account, such as the list of your managed users, is refused with '403' and 'MANAGED_USER_SCOPE_ROUTE_NOT_AVAILABLE': send it without the header. Only your API key can send it. The header is a limit the call asks for: whoever holds the key can leave it out, so for a credential that a customer's browser holds, use an editor session. An 'Idempotency-Key' is kept apart for each managed user. ${YELLOW}Specify as: X-Managed-User-External-Id:value${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e "  * ${GREEN}body${OFF} ${BLUE}[application/json]${OFF} ${RED}(required)${OFF}${OFF} - " | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e ""
    echo ""
    echo -e "${BOLD}${WHITE}Responses${OFF}"
    code=201
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  201;The workflow was created${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=400
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  400;The workspace, the name, the time zone or the composition is not acceptable${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=401
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  401;Unauthorized${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=403
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  403;Forbidden - Not a member of this organization, the plan does not include workflows ('AUTHZ_PLAN_RESTRICTION'), or the call is made for one managed user ('X-Managed-User-Id') in a workspace other than 'personal' ('MANAGED_USER_SCOPE_ROUTE_NOT_AVAILABLE')${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=422
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  422;The workspace already holds as many workflows as it may${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=503
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  503;Workflows cannot be used on this server right now${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
}
##############################################################################
#
# Print help for createWorkspaceWorkflowFromPreset operation
#
##############################################################################
print_createWorkspaceWorkflowFromPreset_help() {
    echo ""
    echo -e "${BOLD}${WHITE}createWorkspaceWorkflowFromPreset - Start a Workflow from a starting point${OFF}${BLUE}(AUTH - )${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e ""
    echo -e "Makes your own copy of a starting point ('listWorkspaceWorkflowPresets'): a copy of every widget it chains (an
ordinary private widget that serves the starting point's published code), a composition of your own on each copy
(a draft, with the content, design, embed settings and tables of the original), and a draft workflow wired like the
starting point's live version. The workflow is named as you ask, or after the starting point. Nothing you do to the
copy reaches the starting point, and nothing its offerer changes afterwards reaches your copy. The workflow stays a
draft: publish it when it is ready.

A start takes a few seconds, because each widget is copied. Send an 'Idempotency-Key' so that asking again after
a timeout makes one copy. When a start fails (503 with 'details.reason' 'preset_copy_failed') the compositions it
made are removed again, so asking again is safe; the widget copies it made stay in the workspace as ordinary
widgets. The workspace's limit of workflows is checked before anything is copied.

A starting point that is not offered to you, or that can no longer be started, is 404.
For personal workspace, use 'personal' as workspaceId.
For organization workspace, use the organization UUID as workspaceId. Any active member can start one." | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80
    echo -e ""
    echo -e "${BOLD}${WHITE}Parameters${OFF}"
    echo -e "  * ${GREEN}workspaceId${OFF} ${BLUE}[string]${OFF} ${RED}(required)${OFF} ${CYAN}(default: null)${OFF} - The workspace: 'personal' for your own workspace, or the UUID of an organization. A call made for one of your
managed users ('X-Managed-User-Id') always uses 'personal': a managed user has no other workspace, and a call
that names an organization is refused with 403. ${YELLOW}Specify as: workspaceId=value${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e "  * ${GREEN}Idempotency-Key${OFF} ${BLUE}[string]${OFF} ${RED}(required)${OFF} ${CYAN}(default: null)${OFF} - Required: a call without it is refused with '400'. A key of your own that names this one request; a UUID is ideal. It is 8 to 50 characters of letters, digits, '-' and '_'. Send the same key again when you retry (after a timeout, a dropped connection or a '5xx') and the call is carried out once: the retry gets the first answer back, marked 'X-Idempotency-Cached: true'. The same key with a different body is refused with '422', and a retry that arrives while the first call is still running with '409' (see 'Retry-After'). ${YELLOW}Specify as: Idempotency-Key:value${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
