}
##############################################################################
#
# Print help for uploadsPost operation
#
##############################################################################
print_uploadsPost_help() {
    echo ""
    echo -e "${BOLD}${WHITE}uploadsPost - Upload a file${OFF}${BLUE}(AUTH - )${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e ""
    echo -e "Stores one file for the account and returns its public address. This is how a user's own images,
video and PDFs reach a widget's content.

Send a 'multipart/form-data' request with the file in the field named 'file'. The file counts
against the storage of the workspace it is uploaded in, and a full workspace is refused with 413 and
'QUOTA_STORAGE_EXCEEDED'. For a person signed in on widgetic.com that is the workspace they are currently
working in: inside a team, the team's shared storage; inside their own workspace, their own allowance. An
organization API key, and a Shopify store's session, always work in that team's shared storage. A personal
API key or an SDK token always uses the account's own allowance. The two never add up and one never lends
room to the other. A file over the size limit is refused with 413 and 'UPLOAD_TOO_LARGE', and a
type that is not accepted with 415 and 'UPLOAD_UNSUPPORTED_TYPE'; 'uploadsLimitsGet' lists the size
limit and the accepted types.

A file is judged by what is in it, not by the type it is sent as. A file that is not the type it claims (a
web page sent as 'image/png') is refused with 415 and 'UPLOAD_UNSUPPORTED_TYPE', and a picture sent under
the wrong picture type is stored under the type it really is, which 'mime_type' in the answer says. An SVG
is rewritten as it is stored: script, 'foreignObject', animation and references to other addresses are
taken out, it must be UTF-8 and at most 2 MB, and the stored file can be larger or smaller than the one
sent. Anything that is not an image, audio or video (a PDF, for example) is served as a download rather
than shown in a page.

When the full storage is a Shopify store's team's, extra storage cannot be added through Shopify yet, so the
message ends by saying so and what to do instead: delete files, or contact support. On a Solo plan it names
the Teams plan (which holds more) and 'error.details.planPageUrl' is the address of the plan page on Shopify.
'error.suggestedAction' says the same in a few words, instead of the usual \"upgrade your storage plan\". Any
other team, and a person's own workspace, get the shorter message.

To upload the file for one of your managed users, send 'managedUserId' (Widgetic's id for the user) or
'managedUserExternalId' (your own identifier for the user), not both. The file stays in your account and
counts against its allowance; the tag lets you list one user's files with 'uploadsGet'. The managed user
must be yours and active: one that is not yours, or does not exist, is refused with 404 and
'MANAGED_USER_NOT_FOUND', and one that is switched off with 409 and 'MANAGED_USER_INACTIVE', before the
file is stored. The tag is set here and does not change afterwards.

Called with an editor session ('createManagedUserEditorSession'), the file is always filed for the
session's own managed user and is always media for widget content: naming another managed user is
refused with 403 and 'MANAGED_USER_SESSION_MISMATCH', and 'contextType', 'source', 'widgetId' and
'conversationId' are ignored. A full storage allowance is refused with the same 413 and
'QUOTA_STORAGE_EXCEEDED', but the message only says that it is not available right now (not how much is
stored: that is the partner's business) and 'error.details.limit' is 'storage'.

An account that administers a partner with a storage destination ('setPartnerStorageDestination') has
its files stored in the partner's own bucket instead. Such a file takes none of the allowance, its 'url'
is served from the partner's public address, and its 'storage_key' is the key in the partner's bucket.
The file is never stored with Widgetic instead: when the destination cannot be used the upload is refused
with 503 and 'STORAGE_DESTINATION_UNAVAILABLE', and when the partner's storage rejects the file with
502 and 'STORAGE_DESTINATION_WRITE_FAILED'.

Partner storage is not optional, and it does not depend on how the file arrives. A partner's own uploads (with
its API key, an SDK token, or from the Widgetic website, the resumable route and the media library alike)
and the uploads of its customers' editor sessions are kept in the partner's own storage or not at all, so a
partner with no destination (or one that removed it after the session was made) has them refused with 409
and 'PARTNER_STORAGE_REQUIRED'; they are never stored with Widgetic. An editor session's browser is only
told that the feature is not available right now." | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80
    echo -e ""
    echo -e "${BOLD}${WHITE}Parameters${OFF}"
    echo ""
    echo -e "${BOLD}${WHITE}Responses${OFF}"
    code=200
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  200;The stored file${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=400
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  400;No file was sent, more than one was, or it was not in the field named 'file'; or a managed user field is not valid ('MANAGED_USER_REFERENCE_INVALID', or 'MANAGED_USER_REFERENCE_AMBIGUOUS' when both are sent); or 'purpose' is not one of the three ('UPLOAD_INVALID_PURPOSE')${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=401
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  401;The API key is missing or invalid${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=403
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  403;An editor session named a managed user other than its own ('MANAGED_USER_SESSION_MISMATCH')${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=404
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  404;The managed user is not one of yours ('MANAGED_USER_NOT_FOUND')${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=409
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  409;The managed user is switched off, so nothing new can be uploaded for it ('MANAGED_USER_INACTIVE'); or an editor session uploaded and the partner has no storage destination ('PARTNER_STORAGE_REQUIRED')${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=413
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  413;The file is over the size limit ('UPLOAD_TOO_LARGE'), or the storage of the workspace the file is for is full ('QUOTA_STORAGE_EXCEEDED'; for a Shopify store's team the message also says what to do, and on a Solo plan 'error.details.planPageUrl' is the plan page)${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=415
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  415;The file type is not accepted, or the contents are not the type the file was sent as ('UPLOAD_UNSUPPORTED_TYPE')${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=502
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  502;The partner's own storage did not accept the file ('STORAGE_DESTINATION_WRITE_FAILED')${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=503
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  503;The account's storage destination cannot be used right now ('STORAGE_DESTINATION_UNAVAILABLE')${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
}
##############################################################################
#
# Print help for validateCompositionContent operation
#
##############################################################################
print_validateCompositionContent_help() {
    echo ""
    echo -e "${BOLD}${WHITE}validateCompositionContent - Validate Content${OFF}${BLUE}(AUTH - )${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e ""
    echo -e "Checks content against the composition's widget schema without saving it. Send what a content update ('PUT /compositions/{id}/content') would store, '{ \"design\": {...}, \"content\": {...} }', or the widget's values alone. Each value is checked by the kind of field the widget declares for it: text, a number within the limits of its slider, true or false, one of the choices of a dropdown, a color, a font, the address of an image, a date. The items of the widget's list are checked the same way, and their number against the limits of the list. A value that cannot be what the field holds, or a number outside its range, is an error and 'valid' is false. Text longer than the field takes, a number or true/false sent as text, and a name the widget has no field for are warnings, and 'valid' stays true. The design is not checked here. Nothing is saved and nothing in the body is changed." | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80
    echo -e ""
    echo -e "${BOLD}${WHITE}Parameters${OFF}"
    echo -e "  * ${GREEN}id${OFF} ${BLUE}[string]${OFF} ${RED}(required)${OFF} ${CYAN}(default: null)${OFF} - ID of the composition ${YELLOW}Specify as: id=value${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e "  * ${GREEN}Idempotency-Key${OFF} ${BLUE}[string]${OFF} ${RED}(required)${OFF} ${CYAN}(default: null)${OFF} - Required: a call without it is refused with '400'. A key of your own that names this one request; a UUID is ideal. It is 8 to 50 characters of letters, digits, '-' and '_'. Send the same key again when you retry (after a timeout, a dropped connection or a '5xx') and the call is carried out once: the retry gets the first answer back, marked 'X-Idempotency-Cached: true'. The same key with a different body is refused with '422', and a retry that arrives while the first call is still running with '409' (see 'Retry-After'). ${YELLOW}Specify as: Idempotency-Key:value${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e "  * ${GREEN}X-Managed-User-Id${OFF} ${BLUE}[string]${OFF} ${CYAN}(default: null)${OFF} - The id Widgetic gave the managed user ('POST /managed-users'). Makes this call for one of your managed users, so that a mistake in your own code cannot reach another customer's work. Send this header, or the other one, never both. Left out, the call works on your whole account, as it always has. With it, the call reaches only that user's compositions and workflows: a list shows only theirs, a composition or a workflow the call makes is filed under them, and one of another user, or one that does not exist, answers '404' (the same answer, so the call cannot be used to find out what another customer has). A managed user that is not yours answers '404' with 'MANAGED_USER_NOT_FOUND'. An empty, repeated or malformed header is '400' with 'MANAGED_USER_SCOPE_INVALID'; an empty header is never read as no header. A call that is about the whole account, such as the list of your managed users, is refused with '403' and 'MANAGED_USER_SCOPE_ROUTE_NOT_AVAILABLE': send it without the header. Only your API key can send it. The header is a limit the call asks for: whoever holds the key can leave it out, so for a credential that a customer's browser holds, use an editor session. An 'Idempotency-Key' is kept apart for each managed user. ${YELLOW}Specify as: X-Managed-User-Id:value${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e "  * ${GREEN}X-Managed-User-External-Id${OFF} ${BLUE}[string]${OFF} ${CYAN}(default: null)${OFF} - Your own id for the managed user (its 'externalId'), when you do not keep Widgetic's. Makes this call for one of your managed users, so that a mistake in your own code cannot reach another customer's work. Send this header, or the other one, never both. Left out, the call works on your whole account, as it always has. With it, the call reaches only that user's compositions and workflows: a list shows only theirs, a composition or a workflow the call makes is filed under them, and one of another user, or one that does not exist, answers '404' (the same answer, so the call cannot be used to find out what another customer has). A managed user that is not yours answers '404' with 'MANAGED_USER_NOT_FOUND'. An empty, repeated or malformed header is '400' with 'MANAGED_USER_SCOPE_INVALID'; an empty header is never read as no header. A call that is about the whole account, such as the list of your managed users, is refused with '403' and 'MANAGED_USER_SCOPE_ROUTE_NOT_AVAILABLE': send it without the header. Only your API key can send it. The header is a limit the call asks for: whoever holds the key can leave it out, so for a credential that a customer's browser holds, use an editor session. An 'Idempotency-Key' is kept apart for each managed user. ${YELLOW}Specify as: X-Managed-User-External-Id:value${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e "  * ${GREEN}body${OFF} ${BLUE}[application/json]${OFF} ${RED}(required)${OFF}${OFF} - " | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e ""
    echo ""
    echo -e "${BOLD}${WHITE}Responses${OFF}"
    code=200
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  200;The check ran; 'valid' says whether the content passed it.${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=400
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  400;The body is not a JSON object.${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=401
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  401;Unauthorized${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=404
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  404;Composition not found${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
}
