}
##############################################################################
#
# Print help for uploadsPost_0 operation
#
##############################################################################
print_uploadsPost_0_help() {
    echo ""
    echo -e "${BOLD}${WHITE}uploadsPost_0 - Upload a file${OFF}${BLUE}(AUTH - )${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e ""
    echo -e "Stores one file for the account and returns its public address. This is how a user's own images,
video and PDFs reach a widget's content.

Send a 'multipart/form-data' request with the file in the field named 'file'. The file counts
against the storage of the workspace it is uploaded in, and a full workspace is refused with 413 and
'QUOTA_STORAGE_EXCEEDED'. For a person signed in on widgetic.com that is the workspace they are currently
working in: inside a team, the team's shared storage; inside their own workspace, their own allowance. An
organization API key, and a Shopify store's session, always work in that team's shared storage. A personal
API key or an SDK token always uses the account's own allowance. The two never add up and one never lends
room to the other. A file over the size limit is refused with 413 and 'UPLOAD_TOO_LARGE', and a
type that is not accepted with 415 and 'UPLOAD_UNSUPPORTED_TYPE'; 'uploadsLimitsGet' lists the size
limit and the accepted types.

A file is judged by what is in it, not by the type it is sent as. A file that is not the type it claims (a
web page sent as 'image/png') is refused with 415 and 'UPLOAD_UNSUPPORTED_TYPE', and a picture sent under
the wrong picture type is stored under the type it really is, which 'mime_type' in the answer says. An SVG
is rewritten as it is stored: script, 'foreignObject', animation and references to other addresses are
taken out, it must be UTF-8 and at most 2 MB, and the stored file can be larger or smaller than the one
sent. Anything that is not an image, audio or video (a PDF, for example) is served as a download rather
than shown in a page.

When the full storage is a Shopify store's team's, extra storage cannot be added through Shopify yet, so the
message ends by saying so and what to do instead: delete files, or contact support. On a Solo plan it names
the Teams plan (which holds more) and 'error.details.planPageUrl' is the address of the plan page on Shopify.
'error.suggestedAction' says the same in a few words, instead of the usual \"upgrade your storage plan\". Any
other team, and a person's own workspace, get the shorter message.

To upload the file for one of your managed users, send 'managedUserId' (Widgetic's id for the user) or
'managedUserExternalId' (your own identifier for the user), not both. The file stays in your account and
counts against its allowance; the tag lets you list one user's files with 'uploadsGet'. The managed user
must be yours and active: one that is not yours, or does not exist, is refused with 404 and
'MANAGED_USER_NOT_FOUND', and one that is switched off with 409 and 'MANAGED_USER_INACTIVE', before the
file is stored. The tag is set here and does not change afterwards.

Called with an editor session ('createManagedUserEditorSession'), the file is always filed for the
session's own managed user and is always media for widget content: naming another managed user is
refused with 403 and 'MANAGED_USER_SESSION_MISMATCH', and 'contextType', 'source', 'widgetId' and
'conversationId' are ignored. A full storage allowance is refused with the same 413 and
'QUOTA_STORAGE_EXCEEDED', but the message only says that it is not available right now (not how much is
stored: that is the partner's business) and 'error.details.limit' is 'storage'.

An account that administers a partner with a storage destination ('setPartnerStorageDestination') has
its files stored in the partner's own bucket instead. Such a file takes none of the allowance, its 'url'
is served from the partner's public address, and its 'storage_key' is the key in the partner's bucket.
The file is never stored with Widgetic instead: when the destination cannot be used the upload is refused
with 503 and 'STORAGE_DESTINATION_UNAVAILABLE', and when the partner's storage rejects the file with
502 and 'STORAGE_DESTINATION_WRITE_FAILED'.

Partner storage is not optional, and it does not depend on how the file arrives. A partner's own uploads (with
its API key, an SDK token, or from the Widgetic website, the resumable route and the media library alike)
and the uploads of its customers' editor sessions are kept in the partner's own storage or not at all, so a
partner with no destination (or one that removed it after the session was made) has them refused with 409
and 'PARTNER_STORAGE_REQUIRED'; they are never stored with Widgetic. An editor session's browser is only
told that the feature is not available right now." | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80
    echo -e ""
    echo -e "${BOLD}${WHITE}Parameters${OFF}"
    echo ""
    echo -e "${BOLD}${WHITE}Responses${OFF}"
    code=200
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  200;The stored file${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=400
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  400;No file was sent, more than one was, or it was not in the field named 'file'; or a managed user field is not valid ('MANAGED_USER_REFERENCE_INVALID', or 'MANAGED_USER_REFERENCE_AMBIGUOUS' when both are sent); or 'purpose' is not one of the three ('UPLOAD_INVALID_PURPOSE')${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=401
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  401;The API key is missing or invalid${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=403
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  403;An editor session named a managed user other than its own ('MANAGED_USER_SESSION_MISMATCH')${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=404
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  404;The managed user is not one of yours ('MANAGED_USER_NOT_FOUND')${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=409
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  409;The managed user is switched off, so nothing new can be uploaded for it ('MANAGED_USER_INACTIVE'); or an editor session uploaded and the partner has no storage destination ('PARTNER_STORAGE_REQUIRED')${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=413
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  413;The file is over the size limit ('UPLOAD_TOO_LARGE'), or the storage of the workspace the file is for is full ('QUOTA_STORAGE_EXCEEDED'; for a Shopify store's team the message also says what to do, and on a Solo plan 'error.details.planPageUrl' is the plan page)${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=415
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  415;The file type is not accepted, or the contents are not the type the file was sent as ('UPLOAD_UNSUPPORTED_TYPE')${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=502
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  502;The partner's own storage did not accept the file ('STORAGE_DESTINATION_WRITE_FAILED')${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=503
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  503;The account's storage destination cannot be used right now ('STORAGE_DESTINATION_UNAVAILABLE')${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
}
##############################################################################
#
# Print help for addPersonalWorkspaceDomain_0 operation
#
##############################################################################
print_addPersonalWorkspaceDomain_0_help() {
    echo ""
    echo -e "${BOLD}${WHITE}addPersonalWorkspaceDomain_0 - Allow a website to show your widgets${OFF}${BLUE}(AUTH - )${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e ""
    echo -e "Adds a website to an account's own list. Give a website name such as 'example.com', or '*.example.com' for a website and all of its subdomains. A scheme, a port, a path, capital letters and a leading 'www.' are dropped, so 'https://www.Example.com/shop' is kept as 'example.com', and 'example.com' covers 'www.example.com' too. Something that is not a website name is refused, not stored.
Until the first website is added nothing is restricted, and a widget can be shown anywhere. Once the list has one, a widget of the account is shown on the listed websites (and on Widgetic's own) and nowhere else. A page on your own machine ('localhost', '127.0.0.1' or '[::1]', on any port) is always allowed, so there is nothing to add to test locally. So is the website where a partner your account administers integrates Widgetic, with every subdomain of it ('platformDomain' in the answer of 'GET /partners/mine'), so there is nothing to add for it either and a list can never lock it out. A change can take about 15 seconds to reach every server.
The list is a safeguard against other websites showing your widgets in a visitor's browser. It is not access control: anyone who knows a widget's id can still fetch its published content with a plain request that names no website.
There is no limit on the list of an account that administers a partner, so a partner can add the website of each of its customers as they publish on their own domain, one call each. Any other account can list at most 50 websites, and the 51st is answered with a 409 ('BUSINESS_STATE_CONFLICT'). A wildcard such as '*.example.com' counts as one website, not one per subdomain, so use it instead of listing each subdomain.
A page that frames a widget can name only so many websites to the browser (about fifty of ordinary length). Past that, the browser no longer checks the list for that page; the lookup that the Embed SDK makes for the widget still refuses every website that is not on the list." | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80
    echo -e ""
    echo -e "${BOLD}${WHITE}Parameters${OFF}"
    echo -e "  * ${GREEN}id${OFF} ${BLUE}[string]${OFF} ${RED}(required)${OFF} ${CYAN}(default: null)${OFF} - The account the list belongs to. For your own, your own user id ${YELLOW}Specify as: id=value${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e "  * ${GREEN}body${OFF} ${BLUE}[application/json]${OFF} ${RED}(required)${OFF}${OFF} - " | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e ""
    echo ""
    echo -e "${BOLD}${WHITE}Responses${OFF}"
    code=201
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  201;The website was added${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=400
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  400;The text is missing, longer than 255 characters, or not a website name${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=401
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  401;Not authenticated${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=403
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  403;The list belongs to another account${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=404
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  404;The account was not found${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=409
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  409;The website is already on the list ('RESOURCE_ALREADY_EXISTS'), or the account does not administer a partner and its list already holds 50 websites ('BUSINESS_STATE_CONFLICT')${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
}
##############################################################################
#
# Print help for confirmUserAdapterConnection_0 operation
#
##############################################################################
print_confirmUserAdapterConnection_0_help() {
    echo ""
    echo -e "${BOLD}${WHITE}confirmUserAdapterConnection_0 - Confirm an adapter address with the code that was emailed to it${OFF}${BLUE}(AUTH - )${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e ""
    echo -e "Some credentials are an email address Widgetic sends a widget's messages to ('confirmation: email_code' in
'getUserAdapterConnections'). Saving one with 'setUserAdapterConnection' emails a six-digit code to it; this gives
the code back. Only then is the address used: until it is confirmed, the widgets that need it are not charged and
their visitors are told the feature is unavailable.

The code works for 30 minutes and for five wrong tries. After that, save the address again and a new code is
emailed (not sooner than a minute after the last one). A code that is not made of digits is refused without
counting as a try.

Confirming an address that is already confirmed answers 200 with the same state, so a retry of a request that
went through is harmless. Saving a different address, or the same one before it was confirmed, starts again.

This needs an API key with full access. The caller must be the account itself or a Widgetic administrator." | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80
    echo -e ""
    echo -e "${BOLD}${WHITE}Parameters${OFF}"
    echo -e "  * ${GREEN}userId${OFF} ${BLUE}[string]${OFF} ${RED}(required)${OFF} ${CYAN}(default: null)${OFF} - The account that keeps the address. For your own, your own user id ${YELLOW}Specify as: userId=value${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e "  * ${GREEN}adapterId${OFF} ${BLUE}[string]${OFF} ${RED}(required)${OFF} ${CYAN}(default: null)${OFF} - The adapter the address is for ${YELLOW}Specify as: adapterId=value${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e "  * ${GREEN}credentialKey${OFF} ${BLUE}[string]${OFF} ${RED}(required)${OFF} ${CYAN}(default: null)${OFF} - The credential's name within the adapter ${YELLOW}Specify as: credentialKey=value${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e "  * ${GREEN}body${OFF} ${BLUE}[application/json]${OFF} ${RED}(required)${OFF}${OFF} - " | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e ""
    echo ""
    echo -e "${BOLD}${WHITE}Responses${OFF}"
    code=200
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  200;The address is confirmed (or was already)${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=400
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  400;A path value or the body is malformed. The body takes exactly one field, 'code'${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=401
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  401;The API key is missing or invalid${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=403
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  403;The address belongs to another account, or the API key has not full access${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=404
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  404;There is no such adapter or credential, an owner may not keep it, the credential needs no confirmation, or nothing is connected under that name (ADAPTER_NOT_FOUND, CREDENTIAL_NOT_FOUND, CREDENTIAL_NOT_FOR_THIS_ACCOUNT, CONFIRMATION_NOT_NEEDED, CREDENTIAL_NOT_CONNECTED)${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=409
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  409;No code is waiting for the address (CONFIRMATION_NO_CODE_WAITING), or another attempt is being checked, or the address was saved again while this one was checked (CONFIRMATION_BUSY). Save the address again, or retry${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=422
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  422;The code is not made of digits (CONFIRMATION_CODE_INVALID), is not the one emailed (CONFIRMATION_CODE_WRONG; it counts as a try) or is too old (CONFIRMATION_CODE_EXPIRED)${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=429
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  429;Too many changes in a short time (try again after the Retry-After seconds), or five wrong codes were given and the code is dead (CONFIRMATION_TOO_MANY_ATTEMPTS): save the address again for a new one${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=503
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  503;Adapter keys cannot be changed on this server right now (ADAPTER_CONNECTIONS_UNAVAILABLE). Nothing was changed${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
}
##############################################################################
#
# Print help for createUserApiKey_0 operation
#
##############################################################################
print_createUserApiKey_0_help() {
    echo ""
    echo -e "${BOLD}${WHITE}createUserApiKey_0 - Create an API key${OFF}${BLUE}(AUTH - )${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e ""
    echo -e "Makes a new API key for an account and returns its secret in 'key'. That is the only time the secret is shown: Widgetic keeps a hash, so a key that was not stored cannot be recovered, only replaced. To rotate a key, make the new one, switch the integration over to it, then delete the old one.
Only a person signed in on widgetic.com can make a key: a request made with an API key, or with an SDK token, is refused with 403. That way a leaked key cannot be used to make a second one that survives its revocation. Make keys from the dashboard; a key can still list, rename, switch off and delete keys.
An 'Idempotency-Key' header is required (8 to 50 characters: letters, digits, '-' and '_'). A retry with the same header and the same body returns the same answer instead of making a second key, and the same header with a different body is refused with 422. Make keys one at a time: two requests for the same account that run at the same moment can overwrite each other.
A key can be limited to what it needs. Send a 'preset' ('read_only', 'content' or 'full_access') or a list of 'scopes', never both. Send neither for a key that can do everything its owner can, as every key made before scopes existed. A limited key is refused with 403 and the code 'API_KEY_SCOPE_MISSING' on anything outside its scopes, so a key held by a build server or by a partner's backend can be given only the part of the API it uses. The scopes of a key are fixed when it is made: to widen one, make a new key and delete the old one. A limited key cannot make, change or delete keys, exchange tokens or reach the administration routes. The list of scopes is in the 'ApiKeyScope' schema.
Accounts with API access (Solo, Teams and partner accounts) have no limit on how many keys they hold. An account on a plan without API access cannot make one (a partner account is not asked about a plan)." | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80
    echo -e ""
    echo -e "${BOLD}${WHITE}Parameters${OFF}"
    echo -e "  * ${GREEN}id${OFF} ${BLUE}[string]${OFF} ${RED}(required)${OFF} ${CYAN}(default: null)${OFF} - The account the key is for. For your own, your own user id ${YELLOW}Specify as: id=value${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e "  * ${GREEN}Idempotency-Key${OFF} ${BLUE}[string]${OFF} ${RED}(required)${OFF} ${CYAN}(default: null)${OFF} - Required: a call without it is refused with '400'. A key of your own that names this one request; a UUID is ideal. It is 8 to 50 characters of letters, digits, '-' and '_'. Send the same key again when you retry (after a timeout, a dropped connection or a '5xx') and the call is carried out once: the retry gets the first answer back, marked 'X-Idempotency-Cached: true'. The same key with a different body is refused with '422', and a retry that arrives while the first call is still running with '409' (see 'Retry-After'). ${YELLOW}Specify as: Idempotency-Key:value${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e "  * ${GREEN}body${OFF} ${BLUE}[application/json]${OFF} ${RED}(required)${OFF}${OFF} - " | paste -sd' ' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/    /'
    echo -e ""
    echo ""
    echo -e "${BOLD}${WHITE}Responses${OFF}"
    code=200
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  200;The key was made. The secret is in 'key', and is not shown again${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=400
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  400;The name, the expiry or the scopes are not valid (an unknown scope, an empty list, or both a preset and scopes), or the Idempotency-Key header is missing or malformed${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=401
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  401;Not authenticated${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=403
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  403;The request was made with an API key or an SDK token (only a person signed in on widgetic.com can make a key), the account belongs to someone else, or its plan does not include API keys${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=409
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  409;Another request with this Idempotency-Key is still running${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
    code=422
    echo -e "${result_color_table[${code:0:1}]}  422;This Idempotency-Key was already used with a different body${OFF}" | paste -sd' ' | column -t -s ';' | fold -sw 80 | sed '2,$s/^/       /'
}
